# Version-controlled Trivy exceptions for the backend container image scan
# (SCRUM-269, User Story 3, FR-007/FR-008).
#
# This is the SOURCE file, reviewed via pull request like any other repo
# change. It is NOT read directly by Trivy -- .github/scripts/security/
# filter-trivyignore.sh filters it into a runtime-only "active" ignorefile
# on every CI run, dropping any entry whose expiry date has passed or is
# missing/malformed. An expired entry therefore reverts to blocking
# automatically, with no other change required.
#
# Format (one entry per line):
#   <CVE-ID>  # exp:<YYYY-MM-DD> reason:<why this is an accepted, time-bounded risk>
#
# Both exp: and reason: are required. A line missing either is dropped
# (fails closed) rather than silently exempted. See
# specs/020-ci-vulnerability-scan-gates/contracts/exception-mechanisms.md.
#
# No active entries yet -- nothing is currently excepted.
